# meta-deploy.list: the queue meta-deploy.bash runs, in this order.
#
# STANDING RULE (CLAUDE/AgentNotes.md): this list is exactly what needs running NOW. Add a
# run when it is pending, remove it once it has run and is done, leave out what cannot
# usefully run yet, then ask the owner to run meta-deploy.bash. Every step a run needs lives
# in the plan's own scripts, so this is the only command the owner is handed. The order is by
# dependency. A plan with none of triage.bash, deploy.bash and acceptance.bash has nothing
# for the script to do. A triage-only plan is run once, read-only. Words after the folder
# name are passed to that plan's triage.bash, both runs.
#
# One entry per line, four kinds:
#   <plan folder>                  its triage, deploy and acceptance scripts, in order
#   playbooks/<path>.yml           a change no plan owns; run as one unit through its own
#                                  shebang, which goes through run.bash, exactly as
#                                  ./playbooks/imports/<play>.yml does by hand
#   <plan folder>/<script>.bash    one plan script, for a step none of the three fixed names
#                                  fits; run as one unit, like a playbook entry, except
#                                  that a script named *acceptance*.bash may exit 2 for
#                                  COULD NOT ESTABLISH, as an acceptance.bash may
#   changed-plays                  every play that has run here and has to run again, as
#                                  one unit: the checkout's ./run.bash --changed --yes, in
#                                  playbook-main.yml order, stopping at the first failure
#
# changed-plays runs WHERE IT STANDS in the list, like every other entry, and decides which
# plays it runs when it starts, so the entries above it have already run (a play an entry
# above ran is no longer changed, and is not run twice). Put it above the plan entries whose
# deploy or acceptance expects the changed plays to have run, which is the usual case, and
# below an entry it must follow. It replaces a hand-copied list of stale plays: name a
# playbooks/ entry only for a play that must run at a fixed point between two plan steps.
# Its description says which changed plays the agent expects it to pick up and why.
#
# A line starting with # is a comment and is the description of the entry below it: it is how
# the owner learns what a run will do, so write it. Blank lines are ignored. Any other line
# that is not an entry is a fatal error naming its line number.

# Plan 00243: the arm64 fixes are on F44, so this x86_64 host re-runs the plays they touched
# (basic-configs, python, rpm-fusion, comms, markless, browsers, toolbox-install,
# AB-dnf-upgrade, claude-yolo and claude-code-consumer, and of the optional plays those that
# have run here: cli-tools, network-tools, photography, qobuz, vm-test-lab, nvidia, displaylink,
# ipu6-webcam, virtualbox-windows and virtualbox-windows-vm-setup). On x86_64 each renders as
# before; the ccy image is rebuilt once for its version label, and intel-media-driver is now
# its own dnf task, already satisfied, enforced on every run.
# The dormant-branch aggregate (Plan 00245): picks up play-claude-yolo.yml for ccy 3.113.4,
# whose every container now starts with --pids-limit 4096 (CCY_PIDS_LIMIT on the host,
# 256..32768, overrides) from the new lib/container-limits.bash. No image rebuild; a running
# session keeps its old limit until it is relaunched. Also play-claude-code-consumer.yml, whose
# ccc now starts its session and sign-in with --pids-limit 4096. And Plan 00173's follow-up:
# play-basic-configs.yml (shutdown-with-update says cc sessions are named, not warned) and the
# Go ccy-sessions in play-claude-yolo.yml (a warning names each cc session as not shown it).
# And Plan 00177 Tasks 7.6-7.8, in the same play's ccy-teams: ccy --teams with a team this
# machine lacks asks what to do (create it, choose another, start without it, or nothing);
# ccy-teams exits only with codes it documents and says 75, 77 and 78 in words; the board's
# KIND of a host seat is cc. The owner's test after it is Plan 00177 Task 7.9.
# And the Go caches (ccy 3.113.4, same play's launcher and ccy-teams): each launch binds
# ~/.cache/ccy/<project>/go for the Go build, module, golangci-lint and go-qa tool caches,
# bounded at 8 GiB and cleared at launch when over; no image rebuild beyond Plan 00243's.
# And issue #220 (no secret on a command line): play-github-cli-multi.yml checks, makes and
# strips the GitHub SSH keys through helpers/ssh_passphrase (the passphrase on stdin, then
# SSH_ASKPASS) and writes no /tmp/.github_ssh_pp; play-basic-configs.yml deploys
# ssh-keys-rekey, now its own SSH_ASKPASS. Of the optional plays, those that have run here:
# nvidia and displaylink (the MOK password reaches expect on stdin, only when a key is
# imported), ftp-camera (the hotspot profile is made in nmcli's editor from stdin, only when it
# does not exist yet, and the camera FTP user password is hashed by openssl and set by
# chpasswd, both from stdin, instead of useradd/usermod -p; it is set only when it differs, so
# the first run reports one change and later runs none), unifi-controller and unifi-firmware
# (the admin password and its hash on stdin instead of environment:).
# And issue #224 (a command reports changed only when it acted): the plays whose command tasks
# now key changed_when on a probe, of those that have run here: basic-configs, browsers,
# claude-yolo, comms (and element-desktop's task file), git-configure-and-tools (its git
# settings now through git_config), github-cli-multi, gnome-shell, markless,
# network-wait-tuning, suspend-and-lid-policy, toolbox-install, agent-bus, and of the optional
# plays docker, lastpass, md-viewer, nordvpn-openvpn, self-update, speech-to-text,
# unifi-controller (the firewall ports are queried and only a missing one is added, and the
# firewall reloaded only then), unifi-firmware, docker-overlay2-migration,
# virtualbox-windows-vm-setup, displaylink and nvidia. A second run of each should report no
# change for those tasks; one that still does is the probe to report back. ftp-camera is the
# play the issue came from: run twice, its second run must report none of systemd-tmpfiles,
# restorecon or the hotspot tuning changed. If the tuning still reports changed, the third
# line of nmcli -g 802-11-wireless.channel-width for the hotspot is not the 40 the probe
# expects: report that line.
# And issue #228 (one owner per managed block): github-cli-multi no longer writes the ~/.bashrc
# block that sources ~/.bashrc-includes, and now stops before any change if that block is
# missing; lastpass writes its configuration block from one task (it asks only when not yet
# configured, so a configured host sees no prompt).
# And Plan 00209 Task 4.1 (ccy 3.114.0, container 2.81.0): play-claude-yolo.yml stages the agent
# team bus v2 member kit (teamchat) into the ccy image's build context, building the binary from
# src-go as committed at HEAD, and the image is rebuilt once for its new version label. Nothing
# uses the kit yet. After it, a ccy session can run
# /opt/claude-yolo/optional/teamchat/bin/teamchat version, which prints the source digest.
# And Plan 00209 Task 4.2 (ccy 3.115.0, container 2.82.0): the end of the container's start is
# the Go ccy-start-claude, built into the image's build context; the image is rebuilt once. After
# it, a ccy session starts as before (with its supervisor and, on a team, its seats).
# And Plan 00246 Task 8.8: play-vm-test-lab.yml rebuilds vmtest (the links, member-address,
# member-ssh --as, lab-network) and writes the lab's subnets into lab.env from the new host_vars
# mapping vm_test_lab_networks, checked against each other and this host's routes. Set it first
# (n1, n2 and n3: IPv4 /8 to /27 ranges no LAN or VPN of this host uses; the example in
# localhost.yml.dist); unset, the play passes and x30-lab.bash below stops naming it.
changed-plays
# Issue #228: basic-configs, the block's one owner, run once after github-cli-multi has stopped
# writing it, so ~/.bashrc sources every include (~/.bashrc-includes/*, qobuz-players too)
# again rather than only *.bash. Its block should report changed once, then never again.
playbooks/imports/play-basic-configs.yml

# Plan 00246 Task 8.8 (the X30 VM lab): read-only host facts for the lab's new point-to-point
# links, a libvirt `udp` interface between two rootless guests. It prints the domain a member
# with such a NIC would have (virt-install --print-xml; no guest, disk or network is made),
# checks it against libvirt's schema, converts it to the QEMU command line, and records the
# virt-install, libvirt, QEMU and passt versions, the host's memory and the lab's disk, and the
# routes the lab's subnets must avoid. It needs no sudo. Its report says which spelling of the
# interface the host accepts, which is what the first `member-up --link` is built on.
00246-agent-bus-v2-landing-and-cross-network/x30-triage.bash

# Plan 00246 Task 8.8, X30 on the VM lab (after x30-triage: it stops the batch when no udp
# spelling is accepted). Boots four lab guests on three point-to-point links (about 6.75 GiB of
# RAM and 28 GiB of disk, checked first), runs stage A's teamchat play against them (never this
# host; the play ledger is off for those runs), issues seats by the relay form under a password
# sudo with the bus guest's outbound ssh blocked, has two workers on different networks message
# each other with the coordinator absent, then moves the bus guest with the team's DNS url.
# Everything it makes is removed on exit. Needs vm_test_lab_networks (above) and a clean
# checkout. Exit 2 is expected today: restore is refused in the production build until DC8, so
# the host move cannot finish; the report in its run directory says which checks passed.
00246-agent-bus-v2-landing-and-cross-network/x30-lab.bash
